What:		/sys/devices/platform/11100000.usb/pm_state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only cached MT6580 MUSB parent system-PM snapshot. gated means
		PHY and parent clocks were suspended; masked means wrapper IRQs
		remain disabled until child context restoration. sleeps/resumes
		count clock-gating and successful clock/PHY recovery. skips counts
		a retained bound gadget (including pre-enumeration);
		error is the last PM callback errno. An unbound gadget may gate
		its PHY. A bound gadget additionally requires an optional MT6350
		VBUS supplier linked by extcon, a successful fresh absent-VBUS
		sample and its independent CHRDET IRQ armed for wakeup. Missing,
		disabled, online or failed detection retains the listening PHY.
		l1_mask is the saved wrapper IRQ mask; phy_off separately tracks a
		PHY reference released during suspend, including failed recovery.
		bound/speed cache the last late-suspend binding/speed snapshot;
		speed can remain stale after unplug/unbind and is not a VBUS
		detector. vbus_ready caches the supplier's absent-and-wake-armed
		result at late suspend. It does not report current cable presence.
		Reading never accesses the USB core or wakes it. This does not
		establish host remote wake,
		physical 26 MHz stop, or minimum system standby current.
